From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gaokun buildbot <gaokun-buildbot@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: add opt-in Gaokun QSEE fTPM validation

Based on Xilin Wu's QSEE TPM transport and SCM type query:
https://github.com/strongtz/linux-radxa-qcom/commit/9c3041295f115df392bf7675bd24685d152f18d4
https://github.com/strongtz/linux-radxa-qcom/commit/e66d8394348465af2c8948457cd62f8cb5b0d4da

Gaokun EL1/EL2 A/B tests show that the firmware-owned control region
requires HLOS sharing even when new kernel buffers use SELF_OWNER.
Keep the generic QSEECOM allocation policy intact and register only
this fixed region through the HLOS SCM bridge interface.

Limit this bring-up stage to non-provisioning commands and explicit
allow_probe=1. Validate firmware addresses and protocol bounds before
accessing shared buffers. Production key-management policy remains a
separate step after cold-boot and suspend/resume verification.

---
diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2065,6 +2065,41 @@
 
 	return 0;
 }
+
+/**
+ * qcom_scm_query_tpm_type() - Query the TPM backend type from TrustZone.
+ * @type: Returned TPM type.
+ *
+ * Invoke the Qualcomm SIP TPM info call. Success or failure of the secure call
+ * is returned by qcom_scm_call(); the TPM type is returned in result[0].
+ *
+ * Return: Zero on success, nonzero on failure.
+ */
+int qcom_scm_query_tpm_type(u64 *type)
+{
+	struct qcom_scm_desc desc = {
+		.owner = ARM_SMCCC_OWNER_SIP,
+		.svc = QCOM_SCM_SVC_TPM_INFO,
+		.cmd = QCOM_SCM_TPM_INFO_QUERY_TYPE,
+		.arginfo = QCOM_SCM_ARGS(0),
+	};
+	struct qcom_scm_res res = {};
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!type)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	if (!__scm)
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+
+	ret = qcom_scm_call(__scm->dev, &desc, &res);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	*type = res.result[0];
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_scm_query_tpm_type);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_QCOM_QSEECOM
 
